    'reports a working directory that is a file as configuration',
    async () => {
      const root = await ownedRoot();
      const workingDirectory = join(root, `${CANARY}-file.txt`);
      await writeFile(workingDirectory, 'not a folder');
      const { events, error } = await turn(harness(), workingDirectory);
      expectRefused(
        events,
        error,
        'HARNESS_INVALID_CONFIGURATION',
        'Claude could not be started because the working directory is not a folder; check the working directory setting',
      );
      expectPrivate([events, error], root);
    },
    60_000,
  );

  // Windows starts processes in a working directory of up to 258 characters (#102). An existing
  // longer one is refused with ENOENT, and from 260 characters its pipes also fail (ENOTCONN),
  // which this run would report as an unhandled error.
  it.skipIf(!windows).each([258, 259, 260, 300])(
../../../../docs/06-harness-integration.md:760:Windows starts no process whose working directory is missing or longer than 258 characters (error 267). Node reports that refusal as spawn `ENOENT`, the code of a missing executable; the Claude adapter's [start refusals](#claude-code-adapter-26) say which operand it could establish (#364). Codex 0.160.0 reports that for a worker command as `CreateProcessWithLogonW failed: 267` (elevated sandbox) or `CreateProcessAsUserW failed: 267` (unelevated). The #102 occurrences came from per-command directories the worker model mistyped, not from GraphGoblin's `--cd`. The Claude and Codex adapters create their `gg-claude-probe-*` and `gg-codex-probe-*` check directories with `mkdir`, because Windows `fs.mkdtemp` fails from 248 characters (247 still works); a name that already exists is never reused or removed, and up to four fresh names are tried. Evidence and the launch comparison matrix: [WP-F5 launch diagnosis](qa/2026-10-19-wp-f5-launch-diagnosis.md).

